# Transfer hook rules on Meteora launches. Append what you need to
# /etc/launchpad.env, then restart launchpad. Never commit or package real values.
#
# A hooked coin is a Token-2022 mint on Meteora's Dynamic Bonding Curve whose
# transfers call Launchpad's transfer hook program (contracts/curve-transfer-hook).
# The program must be built and deployed by the host owner first; Launchpad never
# holds its upgrade authority, the hook authority or any creator key.
#
# Rollout: 1) build and deploy the program with your Solana platform tools;
# 2) set LAUNCHPAD_HOOK_PROGRAM_ID to the deployed program address; 3) run
#    node scripts/check-hook-readiness.mjs /etc/launchpad.env
#    (prints the program id, whether the account is executable on your RPC and
#    the derived accounts for a sample mint and rule set; read-only, never signs);
# 4) restart launchpad. The Meteora launch page then offers the rules section and
#    /api/launchpad/meteora/status reports hooksEnabled, hookProgramId and
#    hookProgramExecutable. Unset = the feature is off and every hooked launch
#    request answers 503 "Transfer hook rules are not enabled on this host."
#    A value that is not a base58 address stops Launchpad at startup with a clear
#    message rather than running with the feature half-configured.
#
# A hooked launch takes three wallet approvals instead of two: the curve
# configuration (Meteora's createConfigWithTransferHook), the hook setup (the
# coin's hook config and extra-account list, plus the first blocklist wallets
# that fit the packet) and the coin creation. A Blocklist rule with more wallets
# adds further approvals inside the hook-setup stage, up to 28 wallets each
# (the launch review shows "step k/n"); the list is sealed by the first trade.
# There is no first buy in the launch itself; the creator buys with a normal
# trade afterwards.
#
# Supply and authorities: a hooked coin is created under Meteora's Immutable
# token option exactly like every plain Launchpad coin — no mint authority and no
# freeze authority from the first slot, so the supply is fixed at creation and
# nothing has to be frozen later. Rules marked "Launchpad route only" (allowlist,
# holder-gated, holder vesting, tithe) need accounts or a payment only Launchpad
# supplies, so such a coin trades on Launchpad until it graduates; the swap that
# completes the curve removes the hook. The creator's allowlist (Allowlist
# rule) is changed in batches of up to 20 wallets per signed transaction.
# Public, read-only lists (the chain is authoritative, Launchpad's record is the
# fallback):
#   GET /api/launchpad/meteora/hook-allowlist?mint=   -> { wallets, count, source }
#   GET /api/launchpad/meteora/hook-blocklist?mint=   -> { wallets, count, source }

# The deployed Launchpad transfer hook program (base58). Optional; unset = off.
#LAUNCHPAD_HOOK_PROGRAM_ID=ReplaceWithTheDeployedHookProgramAddress

# App-only rules: FOMO-only and Pump App-only
# lock a coin's pool trades to one outside app while the coin is on the curve.
# The hook program reads the transaction's instruction list and refuses a
# trade that does not carry the app's MARK, which you name here in one of
# three shapes:
#   signer:<wallet>                     the wallet must sign the trade (an app
#                                       that co-signs every trade it builds)
#   program:<program id>                a top-level instruction must invoke the
#                                       program (an app with its own program)
#   program:<program id>:account:<slot> a top-level instruction must invoke the
#                                       program with account <slot> (0-based,
#                                       0–63) filled by something other than
#                                       the program (a router's commission or
#                                       referral slot the app always fills)
# Launchpad never builds a trade for such a coin before graduation: the coin page
# turns Buy and Sell off and says so. Each rule is offered on the launch page
# only when its mark is named; unset = that rule is greyed out with the
# reason. Launchpad ships no address for either app: take the mark from the app's
# own transactions on an explorer (which wallet co-signs, which program and
# slot it fills) and check it before setting it. The mark named at
# launch is frozen on the coin's record, so changing or removing a value later
# never moves an existing coin. A value in another shape, or with a key that
# is not a base58 address, stops Launchpad at startup with the setting named.
# Honest limit: a mark admits every transaction that carries it, so an app
# that builds the same swap through the same router and slot is admitted too.
#
# The hook program must carry rule kinds 26 and 27 WITH marks
# (the current contracts/curve-transfer-hook: run `cargo test` there, build with
# `cargo build-sbf` and deploy or upgrade the program) before either value is
# set; an older build of the program refuses these coins with ConfigMismatch.
#LAUNCHPAD_HOOK_FOMO_MARK=signer:ReplaceWithTheFomoCoSignerWallet
#LAUNCHPAD_HOOK_PUMP_APP_MARK=program:ReplaceWithTheRouterProgram:account:5

# Already part of a normal install and required here:
#   LAUNCHPAD_PUBLIC_RPC_URL  dedicated mainnet RPC (the Meteora service simulates
#                         every hooked launch, trade and allowlist change)
#   LAUNCHPAD_PUBLIC_URL      https address; coin metadata is served from it
# Meteora launches themselves are configured in Admin -> Tokens -> Meteora.
